; bfsodium ENCRYPT128 : one AES_128 block
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN; aes/shiftrows is PASTED ten times  aes/mixcolumns nine
; aes/addroundkey eleven  aes/xorword forty  idiom/xor8 ten and aes/xtime ten;
; The S box walk is carried INSIDE  two hundred times;
;
; IO  in:  key{16}  plaintext{16}     (32 bytes)
;     out: ciphertext{16}             (16 bytes)
;
; FIPS 197 section 5 point 1; AddRoundKey  then nine rounds of SubBytes
; ShiftRows MixColumns AddRoundKey  then a last round with no MixColumns;
;
; THERE IS NO INTERFACE LINE AND THAT IS FORCED  for the reason aes/subbytes
; and aes/keyexpand128 have none: the walk advances three cells a turn  so
; tools/bffoot cannot bound a footprint and tools/bfexpand will not paste it;
;
; THE LAYOUT IS THE WHOLE PROBLEM AND IT IS SOLVED BY CHOOSING PASTE BASES;
; The state must sit near the walker or two hundred reads pay to travel there
; and back  and it must sit on the IO cells of every routine pasted over it or
; each round pays thirty two moves a paste; Both are had at once because A
; PASTE MAY SIT AT ANY BASE: aes/shiftrows wants its state at base plus
; nought  aes/mixcolumns at base plus 32 and aes/addroundkey at base plus 25
; so with the state at 82 their bases are 82  50 and 57 and THE STATE NEVER
; MOVES FOR ANY OF THEM;
;
; WHAT STILL PAYS TRAVEL IS THE ROUND KEY; addroundkey's key cells are at base
; plus 41  which is 98  and the schedule's window has to live low with its own
; workspace beside it; That copy is about four percent of the block and there
; is nowhere to put the window that does not cost more somewhere else;
;
; THE SCHEDULE RUNS BESIDE THE ROUNDS AND NOTHING HOLDS 176 BYTES; the window
; holds four words  and after the four words of round r are generated the
; window IS round key r  in order  because word 4r lands in slot nought; So
; this file needs sixteen cells of key schedule and not a hundred and seventy
; six  and aes/keyexpand128 stays a separate program for the callers that want
; the schedule itself;
;
; THE ROUND KEY IS COPIED AND NOT MOVED  every round; addroundkey spends its
; key operand  and the window is wanted again to make the next round key; That
; is the rule the round constant broke in aes/keyexpand128 and it is written
; down in HANDOFF now;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x00f  window{16}  four schedule slots; the key is read here
;   @0x010:0x028  the schedule's paste workspace; aes/xorword aes/xtime and
;                 idiom/xor8 all sit at @0x010
;   @0x029:0x02c  temp{4}   the schedule's w at i minus 1  worked on in place
;   @0x02d        rcon      the round constant  one  then xtime of itself
;   @0x02e        g         the cell a copy hands its value back through
;   @0x032:0x061  aes/mixcolumns pasted at 50  so its state cells are 82 to 97
;   @0x039:0x071  aes/addroundkey pasted at 57  state 82 to 97  key 98 to 113
;   @0x052:0x061  state{16}  AND IT NEVER MOVES; aes/shiftrows is pasted at 82
;   @0x062:0x071  the round key  copied here from the window each round
;   @0x072:0x074  group 0 of the walk; ITS TRAIL IS NEVER SET
;   @0x075:0x374  groups 1 to 256  the S box; element k in group k plus one

; the key and then the plaintext  in that order because a read
; prologue may only ever move right
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=31
; ASSERT zero 32:884
  L31
; ASSERT ptr=0
; the plaintext goes up to the state  which is where it stays
  R16[-R66+L66]L16R17[-R66+L66]L17R18[-R66+L66]L18R19[-R66+L66]L19
  R20[-R66+L66]L20R21[-R66+L66]L21R22[-R66+L66]L22R23[-R66+L66]L23
  R24[-R66+L66]L24R25[-R66+L66]L25R26[-R66+L66]L26R27[-R66+L66]L27
  R28[-R66+L66]L28R29[-R66+L66]L29R30[-R66+L66]L30R31[-R66+L66]L31
; ASSERT ptr=0

; ==== the S box is written into the tape  one datum per group ====
; 256 runs of plus signs  33 thousand instructions  paid once
  R117
